WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.055 --> 00:00:11.910
"I just saved a man from execution!" Tom thought, feeling proud.

2
00:00:11.911 --> 00:00:15.505
Now he wanted to talk to the mother and daughter.

3
00:00:15.506 --> 00:00:19.476
They were also sentenced to death.

4
00:00:19.477 --> 00:00:25.983
Looking at the terrified girl clinging to her mother, Tom was filled with compassion.

5
00:00:25.984 --> 00:00:29.610
She was his age or possibly even younger.

6
00:00:29.611 --> 00:00:34.790
What could she have done to deserve the death sentence?

7
00:00:34.791 --> 00:00:39.630
"Tell me, Sheriff. What are these two accused of?"

8
00:00:39.631 --> 00:00:45.995
Tom secretly hoped the sheriff's evidence was as flimsy as in the last case.

9
00:00:45.996 --> 00:00:49.874
"Well, this is quite a strange situation."

10
00:00:49.875 --> 00:00:53.951
The sheriff jerked his thumb at the mother and daughter.

11
00:00:53.952 --> 00:01:01.034
"These two are accused of using their supernatural powers to create a huge storm.

12
00:01:01.035 --> 00:01:07.633
More than forty people have testified about the terrible destruction it caused."

13
00:01:07.634 --> 00:01:10.535
Tom sat back in his chair to think.

14
00:01:10.536 --> 00:01:15.928
Clearly this was not the answer he had expected.

15
00:01:15.929 --> 00:01:19.926
After a few moments, he asked another question.

16
00:01:19.927 --> 00:01:25.267
"Did this woman also suffer from the storm?"

17
00:01:25.268 --> 00:01:29.091
"Indeed she did, Your Majesty," the sheriff said.

18
00:01:29.092 --> 00:01:36.119
"Her house was swept away, and she and her daughter were left homeless."

19
00:01:36.120 --> 00:01:44.182
"It's hard to believe that someone would deliberately cause such damage to her own home," Tom said.

20
00:01:44.183 --> 00:01:48.647
"That's a good point," one of Tom's advisers said to the other.

21
00:01:48.648 --> 00:01:55.719
"The king's very sharp today," the other replied proudly.

22
00:01:55.720 --> 00:02:03.064
By now almost everyone in the room—including Tom—was rooting for the mother and daughter.

23
00:02:03.065 --> 00:02:11.309
"So, Sheriff, perhaps you can tell us how these two caused such a storm?"

24
00:02:11.310 --> 00:02:15.911
"By pulling off their stockings, sir."

25
00:02:15.912 --> 00:02:21.231
This reply was so ridiculous that Tom had to struggle to keep from laughing.

26
00:02:21.232 --> 00:02:24.963
"Really?" Tom bit his lip.

27
00:02:24.964 --> 00:02:30.865
"Has removing their stockings always had this effect?"

28
00:02:30.866 --> 00:02:36.218
"Always, if the woman utters the right words."

29
00:02:36.219 --> 00:02:39.643
Tom turned to the woman and issued a command.

30
00:02:39.644 --> 00:02:43.930
"Use your powers! I want to see a storm!"

31
00:02:43.931 --> 00:02:49.099
All of Tom's advisers—including Lord Hertford—turned pale.

32
00:02:49.100 --> 00:02:54.588
They squirmed in their seats and looked as if they wanted to flee the room.

33
00:02:54.589 --> 00:03:01.095
But Tom was so eager to see the woman's magical powers that he didn't notice.

34
00:03:01.096 --> 00:03:04.851
The woman looked puzzled.

35
00:03:04.852 --> 00:03:10.669
"Don't worry," Tom said. "You won't be accused of anything.

36
00:03:10.670 --> 00:03:17.909
Moreover I decree that you'll both go free, and no one will be able to harm you.

37
00:03:17.910 --> 00:03:24.850
Go ahead, use your powers to make a storm for me."

38
00:03:24.851 --> 00:03:29.402
"Oh, Your Majesty," the woman said softly.

39
00:03:29.403 --> 00:03:33.728
"I don't have any such powers."

40
00:03:33.729 --> 00:03:38.355
"I understand," Tom said sympathetically.

41
00:03:38.356 --> 00:03:41.093
"Your fears are holding you back.

42
00:03:41.094 --> 00:03:45.281
Let me reassure you that I mean what I say.

43
00:03:45.282 --> 00:03:48.562
I don't need a big storm.

44
00:03:48.563 --> 00:03:55.773
In fact, I'd prefer one that doesn't do much harm because I don't want anyone to get hurt.

45
00:03:55.774 --> 00:04:04.225
But make me a storm—even a small one—and you and your daughter will go free."

46
00:04:04.226 --> 00:04:08.965
The woman began to cry, and her daughter whimpered.

47
00:04:08.966 --> 00:04:19.030
"If I could produce such a miracle," the woman said, "I'd gladly do it to save my child's life.

48
00:04:19.031 --> 00:04:22.208
Even if you still sentenced me to death.

49
00:04:22.209 --> 00:04:27.728
But I have no idea how to make a storm."

50
00:04:27.729 --> 00:04:31.611
Tom thought that sounded like something his mother would say.

51
00:04:31.612 --> 00:04:37.544
She would be willing to sacrifice her own life for her child's too.

52
00:04:37.545 --> 00:04:47.409
"Someone give this woman a handkerchief!" Tom commanded.

53
00:04:47.410 --> 00:04:50.234
Then he addressed the woman again.

54
00:04:50.235 --> 00:04:52.844
"I think you're telling the truth.

55
00:04:52.845 --> 00:04:58.628
You and your daughter are free to go on one condition.

56
00:04:58.629 --> 00:05:02.430
That you both take off your stockings.

57
00:05:02.431 --> 00:05:08.330
If you manage to produce a storm, I'll make you rich."

58
00:05:08.331 --> 00:05:11.961
"Oh, thank you, kind sir!"

59
00:05:11.962 --> 00:05:17.511
The woman immediately kicked off her shoes and started to remove her stockings.

60
00:05:17.512 --> 00:05:21.673
Her daughter did the same.

61
00:05:21.674 --> 00:05:29.932
While Tom eagerly awaited the coming storm, his advisers tried to hide their anxiety.

62
00:05:29.933 --> 00:05:36.243
"Are you sure this is a good idea, Your Majesty?" Lord Hertford asked.

63
00:05:36.244 --> 00:05:40.405
Tom raised his hand to silence his chief adviser.

64
00:05:40.406 --> 00:05:50.207
"And if you can make it snow," he said to the woman, "I'll double your reward."

65
00:05:50.208 --> 00:05:53.833
The girl smiled at the mention of snow.

66
00:05:53.834 --> 00:05:57.531
"Look, Your Majesty, a storm is coming!"

67
00:05:57.532 --> 00:06:03.375
The sheriff pointed out the window. "A cloud is covering the sun!"

68
00:06:03.376 --> 00:06:07.576
Tom stood up and went over to the window.

69
00:06:07.577 --> 00:06:12.503
He looked from the cloud to the woman to the cloud again.

70
00:06:12.504 --> 00:06:23.047
"I see that cloud, but—yes, that's what I thought—it's just a cloud and not a storm.

71
00:06:23.048 --> 00:06:27.825
The sun is coming out again."

72
00:06:27.826 --> 00:06:34.687
Everyone but the sheriff sighed with relief, and the woman hurried her child toward the door.

73
00:06:34.688 --> 00:06:45.691
"If your powers ever return," Tom called out, "promise me that you'll come back and make a storm for me!"

74
00:06:45.692 --> 00:06:52.028
"Oh yes, Your Majesty, of course!" the woman said.

75
00:06:52.029 --> 00:06:57.900
Tom grinned while all his advisers shuddered with horror.

